  },
  {
   "tag": "span",
   "y": 4687,
   "x": 756,
   "w": 104,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Test"
  },
  {
   "tag": "figcaption",
   "y": 4721,
   "x": 756,
   "w": 484,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Overall follow-up barely moves (12.1% test vs 12.3% control), but it moves in opposite directions for the two user types: 198 → 278 returns among new users, 900 → 802 among returning users."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 4787,
   "x": 200,
   "w": 574,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "The swap is the most useful commercial detail in the read-out: the test converts more first-time users into a second visit, and slightly fewer loyal ones. If the goal is acquisition, that is a win; if lifetime value sits with returning users, it is a trade rather than a gain."
  },
  {
   "tag": "title",
   "y": 4810,
   "x": 0,
   "w": 0,
   "in_svg": true,
   "hidden": true,
   "text": "Mean first response time by week"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "y": 4974,
   "x": 234,
   "w": 406,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Reading the numbers honestly"
  },
  {
   "tag": "span",
   "y": 4990,
   "x": 200,
   "w": 16,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "05"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 5022,
   "x": 200,
   "w": 773,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Five things a reader should know before quoting any figure above."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 5072,
   "x": 220,
   "w": 478,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Two labels needed cleaning. Ten rows read '实验组 ' and nine read '对照组 ' with a trailing space, so an untrimmed value count returns four groups — 9,004, 8,977, 10 and 9 — instead of the two real arms. Every figure here trims the label first."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 5072,
   "x": 762,
   "w": 478,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Effects are reported at face value. The 4.5-point dermatology drop carries a two-proportion z of −3.35 and the schedule-wide completion difference is 0.08 points; only the former is large relative to its standard error. The other department moves are within roughly one point and should be read as directional."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 5170,
   "x": 220,
   "w": 478,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Response time is missing exactly where it should be. All 903 sessions lost before a doctor answered have no response time; all 17,097 others have one. Averages over response time therefore describe people who got an answer, not everyone who arrived."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 5191,
   "x": 762,
   "w": 478,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "This is an observational split, not a controlled trial. Groups were assigned at entry with no record of the assignment rule in the data, so a department-level difference could reflect routing, staffing or case mix rather than the new queue alone."
  },
  {
   "tag": "li",
   "y": 5267,
   "x": 220,
   "w": 478,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Consultation length only exists for completed cases. All 2,164 incomplete consultations are blank, so the length figures describe completed work only."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 5382,
   "x": 227,
   "w": 989,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "What the data supports: the new queue design halves long waits and cuts average response time by about a third without changing overall completion. What it warns: dermatology loses completions in a way that repeats across all five skin complaints, and returning users come back less often. A dermatology-specific fix — or excluding skin cases from the new routing — is the obvious next test."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 5604,
   "x": 200,
   "w": 1040,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Source: data/data.csv — 18,000 rows, 12 columns, 2024-11-18 to 2024-12-29. Figures are unweighted arm-level statistics computed with pandas."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "y": 5630,
   "x": 200,
   "w": 1040,
   "in_svg": false,
   "hidden": false,
   "text": "Control = 对照组, Test = 实验组. Percentages are rounded to one decimal; counts are exact. Two-proportion z-scores use the normal approximation."
  }
